From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:05:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: "/" searches the notifications in the shade

QUICK_SETTINGS_NOTIFICATION_SHADE_UX: "/ search notifications". In the
unlocked shade, open on its notifications, "/" from a physical keyboard
(on the Q25 an Alt or Sym key) starts a search:

* Printable keys extend the query, Backspace shortens it (a held
  Backspace never reaches a notification row), Enter keeps the filter
  and hands the keys back to the rows, Down/Tab keep it and move focus,
  Esc or Back clear it. With a kept filter "/" edits it, Esc/Back clear.
  Ctrl and Meta chords, software keyboards and a focused text field
  (inline reply) are left alone. Pure policy shade/sable/SableShadeSearch.
* SableShadeSearchKeys runs pre-IME in SysUIKeyEventHandler (the shade
  window root tells it whether a text editor has focus), before the
  focused row, so query letters never trigger the 0301 row commands.
* SableShadeCoordinator adds a final filter: a notification stays when
  every word of the query (case and accents ignored) is in its app name,
  title, text, big text, sub, summary or conversation title; a group
  summary stays while a child matches; a sensitive (content hidden)
  notification matches on its app name only. The Hub priority count is
  frozen while a search filters.
* The query exists only while the unlocked shade is open: closing or
  locking the shade clears it (QSFragmentCompose feeds
  SableShadeState.onShadeChanged), expanding Quick Settings stops
  typing. The compact shade shows the query in a live-region line.
